      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Implementing a Universal Basic Income (UBI) is the only viable path to ensure long-term societal stability because it eliminates the stigma and bureaucratic inefficiencies that plague targeted welfare programs. By guaranteeing a floor for all citizens, UBI directly boosts aggregate demand and incentivizes entrepreneurship, which targeted programs often fail to do due to complex eligibility rules. Sticking with the status quo of means-tested aid leaves millions of low-income workers in a precarious position, undermining the very economic resilience we need to build.",
